summary:
  The list of what a root inherits lets any name through for a type that
  has a list at all.

history:
  A root has members it never declares: main.qml's `expanded` comes from
  PlasmoidItem, `width` from Item. The cross-file check keeps them in
  INHERITED, seven names on 2026-11-12, each found in the type descriptions
  Qt and Plasma install. Widening that list is the quiet way to make a red
  line go away, and a list that admits everything turns the check into one
  that only looks at files whose root is a type nobody listed.

target:
  tests/test_cross_file_members.py

find:
          if member in f.members or member in inherited:

replace:
          if member in f.members or kind in ROOT_IS:

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cross_file_members.py::test_a_member_has_to_be_at_the_root_of_the_file_the_name_leads_to
  and by tests/test_cross_file_members.py::test_a_misspelt_member_is_named_with_its_line_and_the_file_it_was_looked_for_in
  on the shipped files.
